<includeonly>{| class="wikitable source-semanticschemas-sidebox"
{{Category/display-header | category={{{category|}}} | label={{{label|}}} }}</includeonly><noinclude>
Opens the top half of a SemanticSchemas category sidebox: the `{|`
frame plus the heading row. Pairs with `Category/sidebox-footer`.
See `Category/table-header` for the broader composition pattern.

Visual styling (float, width, background, border, shadow) lives in
`resources/ext.semanticschemas.basecontent.css` keyed off the
`source-semanticschemas-sidebox` class, so skins theme the sidebox
through the cascade and Codex tokens supply dark-mode support.

Parameters:
* category - The category name. Required.
* label    - Optional baked display label.
</noinclude>
